1
00:00:00,827 --> 00:00:01,768
[SPEAKER_01]: What is permanence?

2
00:00:02,929 --> 00:00:03,309
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

3
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:14,138
[SPEAKER_01]: Arising is manif... Well, in the sūtra, it says, arising is manifested, ceasing is manifested, persisting or changing is manifested.

4
00:00:18,702 --> 00:00:25,148
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I don't want to repeat myself, but basically, impermanence pertains to that manifested bit.

5
00:00:27,344 --> 00:00:33,987
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it won't be found in actual arising, or ceasing, or persisting, or changing, because those things are all phenomena.

6
00:00:34,768 --> 00:00:37,389
[SPEAKER_01]: And impermanence pertains to the nature of the phenomena.

7
00:00:37,869 --> 00:00:40,710
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

8
00:00:41,431 --> 00:00:41,871
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

9
00:00:47,394 --> 00:00:49,635
[SPEAKER_00]: Persisting while changing as a phenomena.

10
00:00:50,155 --> 00:00:50,395
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

11
00:00:50,595 --> 00:00:53,717
[SPEAKER_01]: And you... Well, arising is already persisting or changing.

12
00:00:54,497 --> 00:00:56,258
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't see the actual origin of the thing.

13
00:00:56,771 --> 00:00:59,474
[SPEAKER_01]: The point, I mean the exact split second.

14
00:00:59,614 --> 00:01:00,755
[SPEAKER_01]: No, you just have a thing arisen.

15
00:01:02,957 --> 00:01:08,562
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, whether it's arising or whether it's ceasing, it's like fading in and fading out.

16
00:01:09,082 --> 00:01:11,224
[SPEAKER_01]: And fading in, it's only a form of endurance.

17
00:01:11,885 --> 00:01:15,108
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the same thing that it's increasing in its presence.

18
00:01:16,109 --> 00:01:17,070
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's the same thing.

19
00:01:17,670 --> 00:01:21,414
[SPEAKER_01]: So it's persisting as the same thing while it's changing, i.e.

20
00:01:21,514 --> 00:01:22,635
[SPEAKER_01]: increasing in its presence.

21
00:01:24,402 --> 00:01:27,845
[SPEAKER_01]: And same goes for fading out, for decreasing in its presence.

22
00:01:29,066 --> 00:01:44,300
[SPEAKER_01]: But the point is, whether you're witnessing with your senses, arising of some, like, manifestation of a thing, like, poof, something just appeared, or poof, something just disappeared, both of those things arise for you in your experience.

23
00:01:44,921 --> 00:01:50,346
[SPEAKER_01]: Assume when you are looking at the actual disappearance of something, that is appearing for you.

24
00:01:51,159 --> 00:01:59,223
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the disappearance in a particular level, external level, but as an experience, it's actually arising, it's appearing for you, it's manifesting for you.

25
00:01:59,844 --> 00:02:04,666
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's that confusion, because we spoke before, between the usages of arising and arising.

26
00:02:05,787 --> 00:02:10,950
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you should really distinguish between arising, ceasing, persisting or changing, and what manifesting.

27
00:02:12,411 --> 00:02:16,833
[SPEAKER_01]: Because arising is manifested, ceasing is manifested, persisting or changing is manifested.

28
00:02:17,268 --> 00:02:22,991
[SPEAKER_01]: So, from that point of view, you could say arising arises, ceasing arises, persisting or changing arises.

29
00:02:24,132 --> 00:02:25,012
[SPEAKER_01]: Ah, it appears.

30
00:02:26,073 --> 00:02:32,337
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're saying it's always... it is always... Impermanence pertains to that manifestation, to that level.

31
00:02:32,357 --> 00:02:39,441
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't pertain to you having to witness a destruction or disappearance of a thing in order for you to know the impermanence.

32
00:02:39,821 --> 00:02:43,223
[SPEAKER_01]: And even the Sotāpanna's insight says whatever has the nature of arising,

33
00:02:43,897 --> 00:02:48,019
[SPEAKER_01]: has the nature of ceasing and knowing the nature means actually that thing is still in front of you.

34
00:02:48,519 --> 00:02:56,643
[SPEAKER_01]: So, far from seeing it being destroyed in order to realize the impermanence, you actually need it to be arisen in order to see it as impermanent.

35
00:02:58,264 --> 00:03:00,165
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why people have a problem.

36
00:03:00,205 --> 00:03:00,605
[SPEAKER_01]: People who

37
00:03:01,393 --> 00:03:06,114
[SPEAKER_01]: Think the practice is like denying nothing's real, nothing exists, see, the science is sure, this is always changing.

38
00:03:06,374 --> 00:03:08,774
[SPEAKER_01]: They basically never allow things to manifest.

39
00:03:09,314 --> 00:03:16,056
[SPEAKER_01]: Or rather, I mean, you can't really stop them from manifesting, but they never discern the fact that things manifest because they're too busy denying them.

40
00:03:17,016 --> 00:03:25,537
[SPEAKER_01]: As a result of that, well, they just completely cover up any possibility of understanding what the real impermanence is, the impermanence that matters.

41
00:03:25,917 --> 00:03:29,558
