42
00:03:35,798 --> 00:03:38,039
[SPEAKER_00]: But what about impermanence?

43
00:03:38,579 --> 00:03:45,321
[SPEAKER_00]: So, things... a thing is arisen, always.

44
00:03:45,341 --> 00:03:47,902
[SPEAKER_00]: There's always this thing arisen, like the five yogis are.

45
00:03:48,022 --> 00:03:49,362
[SPEAKER_01]: There's always a thing manifested, yeah.

46
00:03:49,782 --> 00:03:52,063
[SPEAKER_00]: Manifested experience is.

47
00:03:52,703 --> 00:03:54,604
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that general experience...

48
00:03:54,644 --> 00:03:57,765
[SPEAKER_01]: The only thing that is unmanifested is nibbāna.

49
00:03:59,025 --> 00:03:59,706
[SPEAKER_00]: Is un...?

50
00:03:59,786 --> 00:04:00,046
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

51
00:04:00,446 --> 00:04:03,967
[SPEAKER_01]: The unborn, the... that's... that's something.

52
00:04:05,153 --> 00:04:11,337
[SPEAKER_01]: The ultimate, like, negative of your experience is there, but it doesn't manifest in a sense that everything else manifests.

53
00:04:11,637 --> 00:04:13,077
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why it's like a negative.

54
