00:08:26,971 --> 00:08:27,291
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

108
00:08:29,772 --> 00:08:34,594
[SPEAKER_01]: And see, like, from a completely wrong view, they kind of arrived

109
00:08:34,950 --> 00:08:43,554
[SPEAKER_01]: At the outside of what I'm talking about, when you realize... Because, basically, matter or non-matter, the only way you can know matter is through your experience.

110
00:08:43,954 --> 00:08:46,915
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, obviously, scientists, they deny the validity of personal experience.

111
00:08:46,935 --> 00:08:49,236
[SPEAKER_01]: They generally project it outside as it's a matter.

112
00:08:49,717 --> 00:08:53,398
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a genuine matter that they are accessing and dealing with, not their experience of it.

113
00:08:54,439 --> 00:08:56,740
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, they say, oh, it's a genuine matter that you cannot destroy.

114
00:08:57,880 --> 00:09:04,103
