170
00:13:00,157 --> 00:13:04,579
[SPEAKER_01]: So, things are impermanent not because you can observe their destruction.

171
00:13:04,879 --> 00:13:08,881
[SPEAKER_01]: Things are impermanent because they have arisen in the first place.

172
00:13:09,842 --> 00:13:11,343
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why they will have to cease.

173
00:13:14,124 --> 00:13:15,184
[SPEAKER_00]: It's beyond your control.

174
00:13:16,305 --> 00:13:17,225
[SPEAKER_01]: Like inconceivable.

175
00:13:18,606 --> 00:13:20,487
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you can still conceive a form of control.

176
00:13:20,507 --> 00:13:22,048
[SPEAKER_01]: You say, ah, this is beyond my control.

177
00:13:22,845 --> 00:13:24,946
[SPEAKER_01]: But you can see a sense of control in regard to that.

178
00:13:25,706 --> 00:13:31,348
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you really drill this deep enough, it becomes inconceivable, even in that remote sense.

179
00:13:31,988 --> 00:13:35,350
[SPEAKER_01]: Because all you're going to find is a reason... is things manifested.

180
00:13:36,230 --> 00:13:41,152
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, through that manifestation, you can discern how it's arising, how it's ceasing, how it's persisting, while changing.

181
00:13:42,232 --> 00:13:43,072
[SPEAKER_01]: It's manifesting.

182
00:13:43,292 --> 00:13:44,233
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the bottom line.

183
00:13:45,513 --> 00:13:49,215
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's right there, where you can see, because it's manifested.

184
00:13:50,963 --> 00:13:51,964
[SPEAKER_01]: And even the word manifests.

185
00:13:51,984 --> 00:13:53,305
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, something's shown to you.

186
00:13:53,525 --> 00:13:55,907
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, nothing to do with you, just... it's there.

187
00:13:56,267 --> 00:13:56,367
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh!

188
00:13:57,248 --> 00:13:59,149
[SPEAKER_01]: For that very reason, it won't be there.

189
00:14:00,951 --> 00:14:03,773
[SPEAKER_01]: Not because you can destroy, not because others... not because... no.

190
00:14:04,013 --> 00:14:08,516
[SPEAKER_01]: Simply because it came uninvited.

191
00:14:08,616 --> 00:14:09,117
[SPEAKER_00]: It's birth.

192
00:14:09,457 --> 00:14:09,957
[SPEAKER_01]: It's birth.

193
00:14:10,157 --> 00:14:12,539
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the whole existence, yeah.

194
00:14:12,579 --> 00:14:16,202
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the nature of the five aggregates, to arise and fall.

195
00:14:18,094 --> 00:14:18,915
[SPEAKER_00]: To be manifested.

196
00:14:19,035 --> 00:14:23,658
[SPEAKER_01]: To be manifested to you, on and on and on, until they break apart.

197
00:14:24,779 --> 00:14:28,782
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why, in regard to the five aggregates, you establish that assumption.

198
00:14:30,263 --> 00:14:33,926
[SPEAKER_01]: That they are yours, that you are theirs, that whatever, that you're in control.

199
00:14:34,207 --> 00:14:39,010
[SPEAKER_01]: Basically, that's how upādāna gets involved with... in regard to the five aggregates.

200
00:14:39,050 --> 00:14:44,274
[SPEAKER_01]: But you can't really... Like, the five aggregates are not upādāna, but there's no upādāna without the five aggregates.

201
00:14:46,116 --> 00:14:47,357
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the Chula Veda, I think.

202
00:14:49,386 --> 00:14:53,788
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the point is, they are indifferent to you, the five aggregates.

203
00:14:54,188 --> 00:14:55,548
[SPEAKER_01]: They go their own course.

204
00:14:56,329 --> 00:15:00,871
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's the interference due to the ignorance, not knowing that you cannot interfere.

205
00:15:01,771 --> 00:15:05,193
[SPEAKER_01]: That lack of knowledge is the form of interference.

206
00:15:05,213 --> 00:15:09,115
[SPEAKER_01]: And that interference, in regard to them, can't really change the five aggregates or do anything with them.

207
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:15,958
[SPEAKER_01]: But you can certainly feel the assumption that you are, that you are in control, that they're yours, that they belong to you, that whatever else.

208
00:15:18,689 --> 00:15:19,850
[SPEAKER_01]: But all they do is manifest.

209
00:15:20,510 --> 00:15:22,171
[SPEAKER_01]: And because they manifest, they cease.

210
00:15:24,573 --> 00:15:32,237
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in terms of... Well, maybe we can go to that sutta, 35, isn't it?

211
00:15:33,338 --> 00:15:33,678
[SPEAKER_01]: Which one?

212
00:15:33,979 --> 00:15:34,659
[SPEAKER_00]: Madhyamikāya.

213
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:37,381
[SPEAKER_01]: Which one?

214
00:15:38,121 --> 00:15:39,022
[SPEAKER_00]: I think it's 35.

215
00:15:40,142 --> 00:15:43,845
[SPEAKER_00]: The one with... Do you see this?

216
00:15:46,286 --> 00:15:46,466
[SPEAKER_00]: 39.

217
00:15:46,506 --> 00:15:47,167
[SPEAKER_00]: What's it?

218
00:16:06,069 --> 00:16:18,038
[SPEAKER_00]: It's sort of with the... when that person assumes that consciousness gets reborn, but consciousness passes on from life to life to life, and he says that's what the Buddha taught.

219
00:16:20,140 --> 00:16:22,021
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, this is about the Venerable Asaji.

220
00:16:23,022 --> 00:16:23,762
[SPEAKER_00]: So, do you find him?

221
00:16:25,163 --> 00:16:25,864
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, but...

222
00:16:26,925 --> 00:16:30,187
[SPEAKER_01]: I think, I think, yeah, I think, but it's it's right after something else.

223
00:16:30,487 --> 00:16:31,268
[SPEAKER_01]: I do remember that.

224
00:16:45,086 --> 00:16:46,607
[SPEAKER_01]: Thirty-eight.

225
00:16:46,667 --> 00:16:47,548
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, do you see?

226
00:16:47,568 --> 00:16:48,769
[SPEAKER_01]: Because this has come to be.

227
00:16:48,889 --> 00:16:49,409
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

228
00:16:50,250 --> 00:16:51,011
[SPEAKER_01]: It's thirty-eight.

229
00:16:51,151 --> 00:16:55,475
[SPEAKER_01]: It's, eh, it's, eh, mahātana, sankhāra, sūta.

230
00:16:55,575 --> 00:16:57,577
[SPEAKER_01]: The greater discourse on the disruption of craving.

231
00:16:59,198 --> 00:17:00,219
[SPEAKER_01]: Sat, bhikkhu sati.

232
00:17:00,499 --> 00:17:02,601
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the sound of the, it's the sound of the fisherman.

233
00:17:02,961 --> 00:17:03,702
[SPEAKER_00]: Sound of the fisherman.

234
00:17:08,113 --> 00:17:09,114
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what about it?

235
00:17:10,235 --> 00:17:18,660
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it's... what started with... he has a view that consciousness gets reborn.

236
00:17:19,741 --> 00:17:24,284
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, he thinks it's the same consciousness that runs among us through the realms of rebirths, not another.

237
00:17:24,665 --> 00:17:24,905
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

238
00:17:25,906 --> 00:17:34,231
[SPEAKER_00]: But, in experience, things just are.

239
00:17:34,892 --> 00:17:36,353
[SPEAKER_00]: And so, too soon it's... you've...

240
00:17:37,023 --> 00:17:40,706
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, the only way you can think is to assume it, because it's inconceivable.

241
00:17:42,487 --> 00:17:49,272
[SPEAKER_01]: It's inconceivable to, like, you can't even conceive, like, the rebirth, in the sense of something would be...

242
00:17:49,292 --> 00:17:55,856
[SPEAKER_01]: It's your ideas or assumptions that come as a result of, like, ignorant manifestations.

243
00:17:56,517 --> 00:18:04,883
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, things are manifesting to your five aggregates throughout your life, and you have ignorance in regard to that, and you base these external assumptions

244
00:18:05,370 --> 00:18:08,132
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you think, ah, it must be this that's passing to the next life.

245
00:18:08,472 --> 00:18:23,263
[SPEAKER_01]: But everything, even this, even the idea of this, and the idea of the next life, and the idea of passing, all of that is already fully affected with those wrong assumptions that you have in regard to your own, like, fundamentals of your own experience from the very start.

246
00:18:26,065 --> 00:18:34,412
[SPEAKER_00]: But his view is almost like this passing point between this life and the next life, that doesn't exist, but there's

247
00:18:35,258 --> 00:18:39,060
[SPEAKER_00]: It's all the passing from this consciousness to that, which is a thing in itself.

248
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:40,101
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a thing in itself.

249
00:18:40,121 --> 00:18:44,583
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, we say that the limbo is another realm, so to speak.

250
00:18:44,703 --> 00:18:49,286
[SPEAKER_00]: If someone, you know, if he passed from this life into limbo... Yeah, well, that's another thing.

251
00:18:49,306 --> 00:18:51,307
[SPEAKER_00]: ...between lives, well, that is a life.

252
00:18:51,327 --> 00:18:52,208
[SPEAKER_01]: That's another life, yeah.

253
00:18:52,788 --> 00:18:53,408
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there's always...

254
00:18:53,669 --> 00:18:55,570
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the manifestation of the ego is continuous.

255
00:18:55,910 --> 00:18:58,031
[SPEAKER_01]: But where he is... And you can discern it.

256
00:18:58,051 --> 00:18:58,892
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what the Buddha said.

257
00:18:58,912 --> 00:19:04,395
[SPEAKER_01]: No matter how many lifetimes somebody can remember, whether it's one, five, five hundred, five

258
00:19:05,790 --> 00:19:11,754
[SPEAKER_01]: All they're going to remember is the arising and passing of the manifestations of the five aggregates of one particular among them.

259
00:19:12,054 --> 00:19:15,817
[SPEAKER_00]: But they won't... they can't imagine the in-between.

260
00:19:16,357 --> 00:19:18,379
[SPEAKER_00]: No, because there is no in-between.

261
00:19:18,419 --> 00:19:19,840
[SPEAKER_00]: That's another thing, yeah.

262
00:19:20,941 --> 00:19:25,164
[SPEAKER_01]: In-between exists only between the two things, and that in-between is the third thing.

263
00:19:26,324 --> 00:19:29,967
[SPEAKER_01]: As in-between, as a negative of the both things, it's a thing.

264
00:19:30,667 --> 00:19:34,230
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I meant, like, even the absence of a material

265
00:19:35,227 --> 00:19:40,689
[SPEAKER_01]: Aspect of a certain thing that you're thinking of, that absence is a thing.

266
00:19:41,750 --> 00:19:47,592
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why space is often listed as one of the... with great elements, with consciousness.

267
00:19:47,772 --> 00:19:51,973
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you have four great elements, earth, water, fire, air, space and consciousness.

268
00:19:53,134 --> 00:19:56,255
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if you look at it, there's a very little distinction between them.

269
00:19:57,255 --> 00:20:01,517
[SPEAKER_01]: Because even space, the negative, the absence of matter, serves as matter.

270
00:20:03,791 --> 00:20:09,116
[SPEAKER_01]: And the consciousness is listed within, because the consciousness is actually, in that sense, external, with that matter.

271
00:20:09,916 --> 00:20:24,368
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can't conceive... well, you can conceive, sorry, you can conceive matter, which is more for the understood, eh, but truly, you can't access the matter, but in the same sense, you can't access your own consciousness, because it's on your own.

272
00:20:25,469 --> 00:20:30,634
[SPEAKER_01]: Consciousness is out there, with those four great elements, outside of your reach.

273
00:20:31,354 --> 00:20:32,295
[SPEAKER_01]: So, all you're going to have,

274
00:20:32,860 --> 00:20:34,902
[SPEAKER_01]: It's basically nāma-rūpa.

275
00:20:36,324 --> 00:20:37,345
[SPEAKER_01]: That's all that appears.

276
00:20:38,546 --> 00:20:43,811
[SPEAKER_01]: No matter how remote, how ambiguous, how distant, how abstract, it's still within the nāma-rūpa.

277
00:20:44,352 --> 00:20:49,557
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't have the experience of consciousness in itself, or matter in itself.

278
00:20:49,577 --> 00:20:52,480
[SPEAKER_01]: All you're going to have is conscious matter, i.e.

279
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:54,342
[SPEAKER_01]: the real experience of nāma-rūpa.

280
00:20:54,888 --> 00:20:57,129
[SPEAKER_01]: But both ends of that experience, i.e.

281
00:20:57,229 --> 00:21:03,772
[SPEAKER_01]: consciousness and the matter, are external to you, inconceivably inaccessible, which makes nāmarūpa inaccessible to you.

282
00:21:04,433 --> 00:21:13,237
[SPEAKER_01]: You can just be witnessing it, well, suffering on account of it, or whatever else, but you can't access it either.

283
00:21:14,337 --> 00:21:19,020
[SPEAKER_01]: In its nature, it manifests, and for those reasons, it ceases.

284
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:24,062
[SPEAKER_01]: Just because it manifests, just because it comes from the direction that it's

285
00:21:25,074 --> 00:21:37,665
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it would be like you're wearing borrowed clothes, but you have no idea where it came from, and you have no idea when it's going to be taken away from you.

286
00:21:38,866 --> 00:21:39,386
[SPEAKER_01]: That's your life.

287
00:21:39,486 --> 00:21:40,207
[SPEAKER_01]: That's everyone's life.

288
00:21:41,568 --> 00:21:42,008
[SPEAKER_01]: Entirely.

289
00:21:44,590 --> 00:21:45,251
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that's the thing.

290
00:21:45,351 --> 00:21:47,593
[SPEAKER_01]: Ah, well, like, you know, I can still enjoy borrowed stuff.

291
00:21:47,953 --> 00:21:51,156
[SPEAKER_01]: You could, if you were to know when the person's going to come and take it away.

292
00:21:51,356 --> 00:21:52,677
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I still have two months to go.

293
00:21:53,277 --> 00:21:53,778
[SPEAKER_01]: But you don't.

294
00:21:54,457 --> 00:21:58,558
[SPEAKER_01]: It can be after the next in-breath, and that that's it.

295
00:21:58,819 --> 00:22:01,619
[SPEAKER_01]: It will be taken away from you.

296
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:05,521
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then you realize, oh, okay, I better adjust my plans accordingly.

297
00:22:07,241 --> 00:22:10,122
[SPEAKER_01]: But no people adjust their plans accordingly, or very few do.

298
00:22:10,702 --> 00:22:14,964
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when things are taken away from you, they're always in the, like, in distress.

299
00:22:16,770 --> 00:22:18,631
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you... there's nothing based on...

300
00:22:19,171 --> 00:22:29,076
[SPEAKER_01]: If you don't plan, like to simplify it a bit, if you don't plan anything on account of borrowed things, and those things are taken away, you will remain completely unaffected.

301
00:22:30,596 --> 00:22:35,199
[SPEAKER_01]: So, basically, when death comes, you will be completely unaffected if you don't plan anything on account of life.

302
00:22:36,259 --> 00:22:38,820
[SPEAKER_01]: Because life is a thing that... that's borrowed.

303
00:22:39,360 --> 00:22:42,262
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, death can't be in front of you, and then you decided to borrow it.

304
00:22:43,062 --> 00:22:44,643
[SPEAKER_01]: But you have no idea who owns it,

305
00:22:45,183 --> 00:22:46,503
[SPEAKER_01]: And who'll take it away?

306
00:22:46,523 --> 00:22:47,204
[SPEAKER_01]: At what time?

307
00:22:48,004 --> 00:22:49,484
[SPEAKER_01]: And the Buddha did say something similar.

308
00:22:49,524 --> 00:22:56,006
[SPEAKER_01]: He said, eh... Mara can do with people what he wants, because they come to his territory and use his things.

309
00:22:56,787 --> 00:22:57,567
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's like a bait.

310
00:22:58,027 --> 00:23:00,068
[SPEAKER_01]: So, on account of that, he's in charge of them.

311
00:23:00,608 --> 00:23:01,988
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, what are those things?

312
00:23:02,028 --> 00:23:05,569
[SPEAKER_01]: And you might think, oh, unwholesome behavior is those things, or something.

313
00:23:06,109 --> 00:23:07,070
[SPEAKER_01]: It's much more than that.

314
00:23:08,090 --> 00:23:14,512
[SPEAKER_01]: Those things are your eyes, your ears, your nose, your tongue, your... your whole sense base.

315
00:23:15,029 --> 00:23:17,231
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's kind of like that whole modern surrealism.

316
00:23:17,671 --> 00:23:19,252
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, so whatever appears, it's not mine.

317
00:23:20,093 --> 00:23:23,896
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, funny enough, we're going to say, whatever appears, it's impermanent, because it appears.

318
00:23:24,537 --> 00:23:25,518
[SPEAKER_01]: Hence, it's not yours.

319
00:23:26,939 --> 00:23:27,659
[SPEAKER_01]: And what appears?

320
00:23:27,699 --> 00:23:36,807
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything that you know of, everything that you think of, everything that you might see or hear or think of, it will have that in common, that it will appear.

321
00:23:37,607 --> 00:23:39,049
[SPEAKER_01]: And for that reason, it will not be yours.

322
00:23:40,370 --> 00:23:41,391
[SPEAKER_01]: Or rather, it cannot be yours.

323
00:23:41,831 --> 00:23:42,692
[SPEAKER_01]: Or you might take it, so.

324
00:23:43,873 --> 00:23:44,213
[SPEAKER_00]: Is it?

325
00:23:45,565 --> 00:23:47,826
[SPEAKER_00]: Or he says, everything becomes like a piece of wood.

326
00:23:48,746 --> 00:23:50,447
[SPEAKER_00]: Or a stick goes... Oh, yeah.

327
00:23:50,747 --> 00:23:58,550
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, when he asked the monks in the forest, like, would you, like, well, some of you would probably be... How do you say?

328
00:23:59,970 --> 00:24:06,713
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, he was basically talking about the, you know, people being upset on account of sickness or death, something happening to your body.

329
00:24:06,733 --> 00:24:13,615
[SPEAKER_01]: And he said, he asked monks, would you be upset if somebody comes in these woods now and starts collecting these dried up twigs and branches that fell off the trees?

330
00:24:13,635 --> 00:24:14,996
[SPEAKER_01]: And they're like, no, we wouldn't, of course.

331
00:24:15,739 --> 00:24:17,119
[SPEAKER_01]: There's nothing to do with us.

332
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:19,860
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how you should regard yourself and your own body.

333
00:24:19,880 --> 00:24:23,422
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, literally, this has nothing to do with me, because it has nothing to do with you.

334
00:24:26,403 --> 00:24:33,265
[SPEAKER_01]: But that also requires giving up the pleasures that you gain through that body, which is why it's so intoxicating.

335
00:24:34,065 --> 00:24:35,386
[SPEAKER_01]: And again, there's another sutta.

336
00:24:35,406 --> 00:24:37,526
[SPEAKER_01]: I was about to say it, but there is another sutta that says it better.

337
00:24:37,706 --> 00:24:45,109
[SPEAKER_01]: If this human realm will only be consisting of pain, people wouldn't need much for prompting to go for liberation.

338
00:24:46,266 --> 00:24:46,846
[SPEAKER_01]: But it doesn't.

339
00:24:46,906 --> 00:24:48,667
[SPEAKER_01]: It consists of that pleasure as well.

340
00:24:49,327 --> 00:24:53,888
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is why people get intoxicated and blinded in regard to that which is hurting them.

341
00:24:55,548 --> 00:24:56,268
[SPEAKER_01]: They just don't see it.

342
00:24:57,069 --> 00:24:59,909
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you're intoxicated with little pleasure you get from it.

343
00:25:06,471 --> 00:25:11,552
[SPEAKER_01]: But both are within the nature of the borrowed goods.

344
00:25:14,013 --> 00:25:15,413
[SPEAKER_01]: That you have no permission to borrow,

345
00:25:17,316 --> 00:25:19,416
[SPEAKER_01]: And you certainly have no control how long you can use it.

346
00:25:21,057 --> 00:25:22,557
[SPEAKER_01]: So, basically, it's even worse.

347
00:25:22,577 --> 00:25:23,557
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you think you own it.

348
00:25:26,038 --> 00:25:29,679
[SPEAKER_01]: So, imagine your surprise, when Mahārāja does come and collect what's his.

349
00:25:30,079 --> 00:25:31,059
[SPEAKER_01]: What always was his.

350
00:25:31,639 --> 00:25:36,880
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why there's another... like all the other suttas who often talk about the puppet on the strings.

351
00:25:38,541 --> 00:25:42,522
[SPEAKER_01]: So, all the things you borrow are basically the strings that Mahārāja uses then to pull you.

352
00:25:42,842 --> 00:25:44,622
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you hold on to those strings.

353
00:25:45,885 --> 00:25:48,467
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the puppet is going where the strings are yanking him.

354
00:25:50,969 --> 00:26:04,358
[SPEAKER_00]: But also, even that self, even that person that holds on to other inner things, experience, or that self that is manifest, that must also be seen.

355
00:26:06,616 --> 00:26:06,977
[SPEAKER_01]: Same.

356
00:26:07,057 --> 00:26:09,218
[SPEAKER_01]: You just see everything with the same right view.

357
00:26:09,799 --> 00:26:13,441
[SPEAKER_01]: So, even that sense of self, it's... it's a reason, it's manifested.

358
00:26:13,561 --> 00:26:15,523
[SPEAKER_01]: You can designate, you can... it's real.

359
00:26:16,043 --> 00:26:18,024
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the Buddha never said there is no self.

360
00:26:18,565 --> 00:26:20,266
[SPEAKER_01]: He said, well, basically, there is not self.

361
00:26:20,666 --> 00:26:24,289
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that which you take to be yourself, that sense of self, doesn't belong to you.

362
00:26:26,610 --> 00:26:30,153
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like still being able to see wrong view, but with the right view.

363
00:26:30,353 --> 00:26:30,593
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

364
00:26:31,373 --> 00:26:33,015
[SPEAKER_00]: You have it... you have that wrong view.

365
00:26:33,215 --> 00:26:34,916
[SPEAKER_01]: And that sense of self is actually

366
00:26:35,403 --> 00:26:49,731
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, as Indriya said, it can often be just a sense of an individual, a sense of a particularly unique set of five aggregates, that you take to be like the most personal aspect of your experience, so you take it to be yourself.

367
00:26:50,692 --> 00:26:56,735
[SPEAKER_01]: But no matter what sense of self it is, how strong it is, leave it for what it is.

368
00:26:56,835 --> 00:27:02,999
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't try to deny it or negate it, because there will be again denying the things that you can't even deny.

369
00:27:03,561 --> 00:27:04,802
[SPEAKER_01]: They manifest on their own.

370
00:27:04,982 --> 00:27:07,563
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're trying to cover up the contradiction in terms.

371
00:27:07,924 --> 00:27:10,805
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why people end up being very frustrated.

372
00:27:12,647 --> 00:27:14,988
[SPEAKER_01]: But the point is, no, allow your sense of self.

373
00:27:15,068 --> 00:27:18,250
[SPEAKER_01]: Actually, see your sense of self as a phenomenon.

374
00:27:18,550 --> 00:27:23,413
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, basically, it's other words saying, see your sense of self as manifested.

375
00:27:23,693 --> 00:27:24,774
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it is manifested.

376
00:27:25,274 --> 00:27:28,396
[SPEAKER_01]: In very ambiguous terms, but it's still manifested as such.

377
00:27:29,657 --> 00:27:30,778
[SPEAKER_01]: So, see it like that.

378
00:27:30,858 --> 00:27:31,218
[SPEAKER_01]: And then,

379
00:27:32,721 --> 00:27:34,661
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't regard it as belonging to you.

380
00:27:37,862 --> 00:27:40,883
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, because even yourself... it was... it's just... yeah.

381
00:27:41,123 --> 00:27:41,343
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

382
00:27:41,743 --> 00:27:42,223
[SPEAKER_01]: Nothing.

383
00:27:42,503 --> 00:27:44,624
[SPEAKER_01]: Nothing in your experience you could have created.

384
00:27:47,345 --> 00:27:48,105
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means everything.

385
00:27:48,385 --> 00:27:49,385
[SPEAKER_01]: You can abandon everything.

386
00:27:49,725 --> 00:27:50,645
[SPEAKER_01]: All of it can be abandoned.

387
00:27:50,865 --> 00:27:57,207
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just the idea that something can create things without being a thing itself.

388
00:27:58,067 --> 00:28:01,348
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you feel like, oh, you need to undo certain processes or whatever.

389
00:28:01,930 --> 00:28:05,952
[SPEAKER_01]: In order for it to stop, and then you can really abandon self.

390
00:28:05,992 --> 00:28:06,212
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

391
00:28:06,553 --> 00:28:07,993
[SPEAKER_01]: That's already the act of yourself.

392
00:28:08,414 --> 00:28:09,194
[SPEAKER_01]: You just have to see.

393
00:28:09,534 --> 00:28:12,496
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why at any time you can see the right view.

394
00:28:12,536 --> 00:28:15,858
[SPEAKER_01]: No matter what situation, good or bad.

395
00:28:16,798 --> 00:28:22,801
[SPEAKER_01]: If you look through the whole thing, including your sense of self, and not own it.

396
00:28:22,821 --> 00:28:27,204
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, recognize that you can't own even your sense of self, which is why it's not yours.

397
00:28:28,004 --> 00:28:29,605
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is not self.

398
00:28:30,417 --> 00:28:38,163
[SPEAKER_01]: There is that which you take to be self, but it's not yourself.

399
00:28:38,303 --> 00:28:41,026
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what that sutra is about, isn't it?

400
00:28:41,726 --> 00:28:43,668
[SPEAKER_00]: When it continues, it's about, do you see this?

401
00:28:44,889 --> 00:28:47,091
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, yeah, it comes back to the very fundamental nature.

402
00:28:47,231 --> 00:28:49,112
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you see this as manifested?

403
00:28:49,913 --> 00:28:50,834
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, Venerable Sir.

404
00:28:51,454 --> 00:28:54,237
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you see it manifested with this as a condition?

405
00:28:55,137 --> 00:28:55,958
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, Venerable Sir.

406
00:28:56,578 --> 00:28:59,541
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you see it with the disappearance of that condition?

407
00:29:00,903 --> 00:29:04,224
[SPEAKER_01]: What has come, what is manifested, has come to cessation.

408
00:29:04,464 --> 00:29:05,885
[SPEAKER_01]: Like this, this remains standing.

409
00:29:08,365 --> 00:29:11,506
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you need to introduce that, like, a determination.

410
00:29:11,566 --> 00:29:16,588
[SPEAKER_01]: I do see this as a condition of the manifested thing, while you're seeing the manifested thing.

411
00:29:17,108 --> 00:29:19,669
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not an explanation of a linear causality.

412
00:29:20,449 --> 00:29:25,471
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, this A creates B and I'm watching both, thus I'm not myself.

413
00:29:26,011 --> 00:29:30,232
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, and that's just complete magical thinking, where you project, okay, so what does that mean?

414
00:29:31,015 --> 00:29:33,757
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, oh, all the things are impermanent and constantly changing.

415
00:29:33,777 --> 00:29:39,402
[SPEAKER_01]: The scientists say the atoms and molecules are never in one, electrons are never in the same spot, da-da-da.

416
00:29:39,943 --> 00:29:40,183
[SPEAKER_01]: So?

417
00:29:41,464 --> 00:29:49,010
[SPEAKER_01]: I still suffer on account of unfulfilled desires, on account of being paired with people I don't want to be paired, being separated from people I don't want to be separated from.

418
00:29:49,651 --> 00:29:52,874
[SPEAKER_01]: No matter what scientific view I might do, it doesn't pertain to you.

419
00:29:53,814 --> 00:29:56,437
[SPEAKER_01]: But, if you see it, all those things are manifested.

420
00:29:57,289 --> 00:30:02,834
[SPEAKER_01]: When I say manifested by oneself, on their own, it means determined by something other than you.

421
00:30:04,115 --> 00:30:08,479
[SPEAKER_01]: Yet, the entire manifestation is completely out of your hands.

422
00:30:10,040 --> 00:30:17,486
[SPEAKER_01]: And if that's the direction where they came from, that determination, these fears, they cannot possibly stay.

423
00:30:17,647 --> 00:30:18,768
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, you're gone.

424
00:30:19,028 --> 00:30:20,209
[SPEAKER_01]: Your experience is taken away.

425
00:30:20,229 --> 00:30:24,873
[SPEAKER_00]: So he says, do you see it as determined by something else?

426
00:30:25,469 --> 00:30:29,631
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, in this particular sutta, he uses the nutriment.

427
00:30:29,812 --> 00:30:30,832
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you see its nutriment?

428
00:30:31,352 --> 00:30:31,553
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

429
00:30:31,773 --> 00:30:36,595
[SPEAKER_00]: And its nutriment is something that you don't necessarily see particularly.

430
00:30:36,776 --> 00:30:42,379
[SPEAKER_01]: No, because that wouldn't be a nutriment, it would be another thing that's now nurtured by something else.

431
00:30:42,759 --> 00:30:51,564
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why I say, while you're aware of the manifested thing, within that manifested thing, you can discern its nutriment.

432
00:30:52,525 --> 00:30:53,185
[SPEAKER_01]: But not by

433
00:30:54,187 --> 00:30:56,988
[SPEAKER_01]: Looking away from the manifested thing and then... Why?

434
00:30:57,028 --> 00:31:03,449
[SPEAKER_01]: Because then you will be looking at another manifested thing that you will think is the nutriment of the previous manifested thing.

435
00:31:03,469 --> 00:31:08,050
[SPEAKER_01]: So, see how you kind of squeezed yourself out and made this whole relationship external.

436
00:31:11,270 --> 00:31:12,911
[SPEAKER_01]: If it's external, it won't be the right view.

437
00:31:14,351 --> 00:31:15,551
[SPEAKER_01]: Needs to arise internally.

438
00:31:15,971 --> 00:31:18,392
[SPEAKER_01]: So, needs to arise within the manifested thing.

439
00:31:19,752 --> 00:31:23,933
[SPEAKER_01]: The nutriment would be then the real nutriment because you haven't abandoned the manifested thing.

440
00:31:26,882 --> 00:31:28,183
[SPEAKER_00]: Can we talk about this?

441
00:31:29,144 --> 00:31:32,186
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not A and B.

442
00:31:33,027 --> 00:31:35,489
[SPEAKER_01]: It's A and smaller A.

443
00:31:36,990 --> 00:31:37,771
[SPEAKER_00]: Within that A.

444
00:31:38,472 --> 00:31:42,895
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the general experience and particular things inside it.

445
00:31:43,276 --> 00:31:43,576
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure.

446
00:31:44,977 --> 00:31:46,318
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's a very general thing to put.

447
00:31:48,160 --> 00:31:50,322
[SPEAKER_01]: To put it that way, it's just like... Too general?

448
00:31:50,642 --> 00:31:51,082
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, no.

449
00:31:51,162 --> 00:31:53,144
[SPEAKER_01]: When you say it's just general and particular, sure.

450
00:31:53,164 --> 00:31:55,046
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's too general as an explanation.

451
00:31:55,366 --> 00:31:55,506
[SPEAKER_01]: Ah.

452
00:31:57,577 --> 00:32:06,240
[SPEAKER_01]: Because... Well, again, general thing can become particular, if you forget about it as general, and then, you know, you rather experience it more generally in regard to it.

453
00:32:06,820 --> 00:32:08,441
[SPEAKER_01]: And you still think you think of general thing.

454
00:32:09,241 --> 00:32:10,442
[SPEAKER_01]: Means whatever is manifested.

455
00:32:11,702 --> 00:32:13,603
[SPEAKER_01]: Any of the aggregates, whatever is manifested.

456
00:32:14,923 --> 00:32:20,705
[SPEAKER_01]: Or you can just go, as we spoke before, the presence of your body, the presence of your mind.

457
00:32:20,865 --> 00:32:22,986
[SPEAKER_01]: Two simultaneous things, inseparable from.

458
00:32:24,608 --> 00:32:27,569
[SPEAKER_01]: But you can see, when you think about the body, well, that's a mental image.

459
00:32:28,909 --> 00:32:29,589
[SPEAKER_01]: Your own body...

460
00:32:30,029 --> 00:32:32,349
[SPEAKER_01]: So, everything shares the nature of a mental image.

461
00:32:33,029 --> 00:32:33,610
[SPEAKER_01]: And what does that mean?

462
00:32:34,330 --> 00:32:35,350
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything is manifested.

463
00:32:35,610 --> 00:32:37,810
[SPEAKER_01]: Because everything manifests on the level of a mental image.

464
00:32:39,311 --> 00:32:45,392
[SPEAKER_01]: So, while you have the mental image of that certain thing, you discern its nutriment within that.

465
00:32:46,152 --> 00:32:52,753
[SPEAKER_01]: And discerning its nutriment means discerning it as coming from something other than your assumed sense of self.

466
00:32:55,219 --> 00:33:00,881
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why you said, like, you need to see a thing, depending upon something else, that cannot be yours.

467
00:33:02,562 --> 00:33:12,466
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, that thing that is yours will be disowned, because you realize, actually, I can't own this, because if that thing, that I cannot own, disappears, this thing will not standing.

468
00:33:12,487 --> 00:33:16,588
[SPEAKER_01]: So, actually, that thing belongs to the other, belongs to its nutriment.

469
00:33:17,229 --> 00:33:21,991
[SPEAKER_01]: It cannot belong to me, because I have no say in its appearance, I have no say in its disappearance.

470
00:33:23,431 --> 00:33:25,052
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this, yeah, this has appeared

471
00:33:28,010 --> 00:33:36,917
[SPEAKER_00]: Because of that, because of which this has appeared.

472
00:33:38,038 --> 00:33:49,948
[SPEAKER_00]: Like this experience, this mental experience, this experience of nāma, rūpa, its nutriments, its... Well, we can speak about it.

473
00:33:50,048 --> 00:33:51,529
[SPEAKER_01]: We can say the experience of self.

474
00:33:53,011 --> 00:33:56,013
[SPEAKER_01]: That I said, self is a manifested phenomenon.

475
00:33:57,677 --> 00:34:01,680
[SPEAKER_01]: That you confuse to... well, that you conceive to belong to you, but it's on the outside.

476
00:34:02,361 --> 00:34:09,006
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can take your sense of self, that ambiguous sense of self, and it's manifested.

477
00:34:09,106 --> 00:34:16,492
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you need to discern its manifestation, whether it's through increasing its presence, decreasing its presence, or simply persisting either way.

478
00:34:18,814 --> 00:34:26,540
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you become skilled in, like, discerning manifestation, picking up the signs of things, that's like picking up the signs of your mind, cittanimitta,

479
00:34:28,227 --> 00:34:34,549
[SPEAKER_01]: Within that, then, when you think about, okay, what is this thing inseparable from?

480
00:34:35,350 --> 00:34:36,870
[SPEAKER_01]: What is a necessary condition?

481
00:34:36,930 --> 00:34:37,971
[SPEAKER_01]: What is a nutriment?

482
00:34:38,131 --> 00:34:40,732
[SPEAKER_01]: What is a basis for this sense of self to be here?

483
00:34:42,332 --> 00:34:55,017
[SPEAKER_01]: But then you have to, like yoniso manasikāra, the root, the womb, attention, means exactly that, goes to the root of the present thing, not to the root of another thing, of another experience.

484
00:34:55,808 --> 00:35:09,336
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why you need that proper attention to discern within the present manifestation, to discern its conditions, or formations, or determinations, or saṅkhara, whatever you want to translate it.

485
00:35:10,657 --> 00:35:20,422
[SPEAKER_01]: So, without abandoning the manifested sense of self that you're mindful of, you need to discern within that, what is that sense of self inseparable from?

486
00:35:23,244 --> 00:35:25,065
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, whatever you find would

487
00:35:25,857 --> 00:35:53,416
[SPEAKER_01]: Will, most likely, be a determination of the thing, unless you over-intended, or rather over-attended, that manifestation in looking for its nutriment, and then found other things that then became manifestations, and they themselves have their own nutriments within themselves that you have not seen, because your attention hasn't been trained to look through things, through a reason phenomenon.

488
00:35:59,022 --> 00:36:00,942
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I was talking about in the Appearance and Existence.

489
00:36:00,982 --> 00:36:03,743
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like turning a sleeve inside out.

490
00:36:04,423 --> 00:36:06,003
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like the same thing.

491
00:36:06,023 --> 00:36:07,404
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just inside out.

492
00:36:08,344 --> 00:36:11,744
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you have to go through it, pick up the other end, and then pull it out.

493
00:36:13,085 --> 00:36:18,766
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why the suttas refer to it like, you know, cutting deep with the probe, with the knife, and then pulling this thing out.

494
00:36:19,206 --> 00:36:20,386
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything else stays the same.

495
00:36:20,406 --> 00:36:26,587
[SPEAKER_01]: Just that one bit, that one misunderstanding at the very root, covers and sort of poisons everything else.

496
00:36:32,310 --> 00:36:33,631
[SPEAKER_01]: So, back on the sense of self.

497
00:36:35,331 --> 00:36:38,653
[SPEAKER_01]: What is it inseparable from, while that sense of self is present?

498
00:36:38,733 --> 00:36:42,915
[SPEAKER_01]: Within that sense of self discern, what is inseparable from?

499
00:36:43,895 --> 00:36:49,457
[SPEAKER_01]: Could you have sense of self present, without being able to think?

500
00:36:50,558 --> 00:36:55,000
[SPEAKER_01]: Without having any mental images whatsoever, would you be able to discern that ambiguous sense of self in me?

501
00:36:57,481 --> 00:36:57,921
[SPEAKER_01]: You wouldn't.

502
00:36:59,162 --> 00:37:00,182
[SPEAKER_01]: So, would you be able to think?

503
00:37:01,458 --> 00:37:07,484
[SPEAKER_01]: If there is no living body that is still operating and paired with consciousness out there in the world, you wouldn't.

504
00:37:09,325 --> 00:37:25,740
[SPEAKER_01]: So then, if that living body paired because you were able to think, you wouldn't be able to have the sense of self, so then there wouldn't be a sense of self in that sense that would belong to you, because if something would happen to that body, something would happen to that consciousness, if something to happen to that ability to think, that sense of self goes.

505
00:37:26,416 --> 00:37:31,538
[SPEAKER_01]: You see, you can see all that, like, on a board.

506
00:37:31,678 --> 00:37:42,423
[SPEAKER_01]: You can write it down as a chart, and it will all make good sense, explanation, but it will not be open-eyed, and it will certainly not free you from suffering or bring you closer to it.

507
00:37:42,483 --> 00:37:42,723
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

508
00:37:42,763 --> 00:37:45,124
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you're not seeing it in the right order.

509
00:37:45,924 --> 00:37:48,465
[SPEAKER_01]: And by the right order, I mean, you don't... you're seeing it linearly.

510
00:37:48,485 --> 00:37:53,067
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't see one within the other.

511
00:37:53,107 --> 00:37:54,428
[SPEAKER_01]: Not next to... or while.

512
00:37:55,372 --> 00:37:57,593
[SPEAKER_01]: One, while the other is still present.

513
00:37:59,174 --> 00:38:04,937
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're seeing it left and right, up or down, but you're not seeing it within that thing.

514
00:38:08,298 --> 00:38:08,619
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

515
00:38:09,119 --> 00:38:11,220
[SPEAKER_00]: You take the self, for example.

516
00:38:11,740 --> 00:38:17,983
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why the whole, the whole ābhidhāma and the commentary is... that's why the entire attitude, the entire way of looking is completely wrong.

517
00:38:20,064 --> 00:38:23,766
[SPEAKER_01]: You... all the stuff from the suttas are there, rich and littered, like packed,

518
00:38:24,578 --> 00:38:25,399
[SPEAKER_01]: It lists and stuff.

519
00:38:25,899 --> 00:38:26,780
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's all linear.

520
00:38:27,060 --> 00:38:28,842
[SPEAKER_01]: It's all out there that you can observe.

521
00:38:31,224 --> 00:38:34,547
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why there's always a reason, the order of things the Buddha would do.

522
00:38:34,567 --> 00:38:36,508
[SPEAKER_01]: He wouldn't just list things out to you.

523
00:38:36,528 --> 00:38:37,749
[SPEAKER_00]: He would be like this.

524
00:38:38,270 --> 00:38:39,451
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you see this has come to be?

525
00:38:39,771 --> 00:38:40,031
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

526
00:38:40,552 --> 00:38:47,238
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, that you see that this has come to be, that sense of self I'm talking about right now, that it's manifested, that you see it for what it is, yeah?

527
00:38:47,618 --> 00:38:49,900
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you see it inseparable from certain nutrients?

528
00:38:50,880 --> 00:38:55,604
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, it would not be able to occur... it would not be able to even be conceived without those nutriments present.

529
00:38:56,565 --> 00:38:57,666
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, Lord, we see that.

530
00:38:59,147 --> 00:39:06,374
[SPEAKER_01]: So, would you see that with the cessation of those nutriments, this will not remain standing even for a split second, inconceivable.

531
00:39:06,574 --> 00:39:08,075
[SPEAKER_01]: Like the two sticks holding each other.

532
00:39:08,096 --> 00:39:09,677
[SPEAKER_01]: You move one, the other one goes down.

533
00:39:10,593 --> 00:39:11,513
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, Lord, we see.

534
00:39:12,013 --> 00:39:18,775
[SPEAKER_01]: And then he refers to that because this view is the purified and bright view as it is.

535
00:39:18,935 --> 00:39:22,576
[SPEAKER_01]: Basically, just that principle is the right view.

536
00:39:23,836 --> 00:39:24,337
[SPEAKER_01]: Nothing else.

537
00:39:24,937 --> 00:39:33,359
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why the kind of generic term for the right view is like, ah, whatever has the nature of arising has the nature of ceasing.

538
00:39:33,919 --> 00:39:37,240
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever is manifested will have to cease, basically, because it's manifested.

539
00:39:39,547 --> 00:39:45,712
[SPEAKER_01]: And then he said, even that view, as pure, as bright, like, you abandon even that.

540
00:39:46,713 --> 00:39:50,936
[SPEAKER_01]: By using that view, you abandon all the wrong views, and then you just let go even of that view.

541
00:39:51,957 --> 00:40:02,146
[SPEAKER_01]: And then the dhamma is truly taught as the, like, as a simile of the raft, and so on.

542
00:40:02,166 --> 00:40:06,089
[SPEAKER_00]: So, to take the sense of self again, why does this manifest?

543
00:40:06,909 --> 00:40:07,410
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it is.

544
00:40:11,910 --> 00:40:14,531
[SPEAKER_00]: It's almost like you keep this in front.

545
00:40:14,871 --> 00:40:15,151
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

546
00:40:15,271 --> 00:40:20,093
[SPEAKER_00]: But then you look at the whole... the two sides at the same time.

547
00:40:20,214 --> 00:40:25,276
[SPEAKER_01]: But then start distinguishing the sides as within that front you're keeping.

548
00:40:25,296 --> 00:40:25,596
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

549
00:40:25,876 --> 00:40:26,456
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not...

550
00:40:26,556 --> 00:40:27,216
[SPEAKER_00]: I can't explain.

551
00:40:27,256 --> 00:40:27,497
[SPEAKER_00]: I know.

552
00:40:27,797 --> 00:40:28,977
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's not spatial.

553
00:40:29,017 --> 00:40:29,217
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

554
00:40:29,337 --> 00:40:30,438
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't pertain to space.

555
00:40:32,219 --> 00:40:32,959
[SPEAKER_01]: But I know what you mean.

556
00:40:32,999 --> 00:40:33,879
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm just saying...

557
00:40:33,899 --> 00:40:34,359
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the same.

558
00:40:34,880 --> 00:40:38,141
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why it's so easy to confuse what comes first, what comes second.

559
00:40:39,982 --> 00:40:40,182
[SPEAKER_01]: It's...

560
00:40:41,573 --> 00:40:42,993
[SPEAKER_01]: It's kind of the same, on the same level.

561
00:40:43,694 --> 00:40:46,915
[SPEAKER_01]: But there is first, there is second, depending on what you attend.

562
00:40:49,256 --> 00:41:01,560
[SPEAKER_01]: So, as I said, you can over-attend and then start attending those supposed nutriments of your sense of self as separate senses of self, as separate things that you just took to be yours.

563
00:41:04,240 --> 00:41:06,241
[SPEAKER_01]: But no, you want to have that thing in front of you.

564
00:41:08,062 --> 00:41:08,682
[SPEAKER_01]: Sense of self

565
00:41:09,828 --> 00:41:16,852
[SPEAKER_01]: Within this very present sense of self, you discern things without abandoning.

566
00:41:17,212 --> 00:41:26,677
[SPEAKER_01]: So, while you're mindful of the sense of self, within that mindfulness of the sense of self, you discern things that this sense of self isn't separable from, as sense of self.

567
00:41:28,998 --> 00:41:29,518
[SPEAKER_00]: It probably isn't.

568
00:41:30,058 --> 00:41:33,320
[SPEAKER_01]: And, like, see, then we'll be overdoing it.

569
00:41:33,993 --> 00:41:35,875
[SPEAKER_01]: You can call it later, five hundred years.

570
00:41:36,195 --> 00:41:45,585
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why, like, Nibiru said, ah, well, like, somebody might not necessarily use the twelve-factored explanation, but did some part, because all they see is, with this, this is.

571
00:41:46,085 --> 00:41:46,546
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's it.

572
00:41:46,606 --> 00:41:47,447
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I'm talking about.

573
00:41:47,487 --> 00:41:48,988
[SPEAKER_01]: With this, this is.

574
00:41:49,449 --> 00:41:51,131
[SPEAKER_01]: So, with these nutriments, this is.

575
00:41:51,972 --> 00:41:53,293
[SPEAKER_01]: But you see it in reverse order.

576
00:41:54,865 --> 00:42:02,908
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, later, you can start discerning more and more where you become proficient in that principle, as when there were non-believers who said, oh, this is so easy, you see it all the time.

577
00:42:02,928 --> 00:42:16,092
[SPEAKER_01]: People said, no, don't say that, because, like, for the very reason people don't see that, which you find easy now, they remain bound to saṃsara for, like, well, intolerable amounts of times.

578
00:42:25,695 --> 00:42:28,796
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, I mean, I can enable my sense of self now.

579
00:42:29,816 --> 00:42:31,917
[SPEAKER_00]: What is it with the sense of self?

580
00:42:33,177 --> 00:42:34,078
[SPEAKER_00]: What is this nutriment?

581
00:42:34,938 --> 00:42:45,521
[SPEAKER_01]: I can see... You can simplify it, but as long as you do it right, like according to... Well, as long as you do the principle right, you can simplify it as you want in terms of designation.

582
00:42:45,921 --> 00:42:48,062
[SPEAKER_01]: You can just say with this, this.

583
00:42:49,362 --> 00:42:52,423
[SPEAKER_01]: But in your mind, see thing within a thing.

584
00:42:53,818 --> 00:42:57,499
[SPEAKER_01]: Not thing next to the thing, not thing before the thing, not thing after the thing.

585
00:42:58,179 --> 00:43:00,739
[SPEAKER_01]: Thing within the present thing.

586
00:43:01,539 --> 00:43:02,800
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why it's akālika.

587
00:43:02,860 --> 00:43:03,640
[SPEAKER_01]: It's timeless.

588
00:43:04,760 --> 00:43:09,741
[SPEAKER_01]: Does not pertain to time, because it's one within the other, simultaneously present.

589
00:43:13,402 --> 00:43:14,622
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I learned in the past.

590
00:43:14,722 --> 00:43:20,563
[SPEAKER_01]: I remember using saying, like, when it feels like a thought, a thought closes upon itself.

591
00:43:21,498 --> 00:43:34,689
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you don't go left, you don't go right, you don't go to another thought, you have a thought present, whatever shape or form, and within that, you sort of, well, let it go, in a sense, see it impossible to own.

592
00:43:34,749 --> 00:43:40,914
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you have no, like, well, not as you have no idea where it came from, it's just the direction of its origin is just inconceivable.

593
00:43:40,954 --> 00:43:42,235
[SPEAKER_01]: So you just have a thing that isn't.

594
00:43:43,416 --> 00:43:46,659
[SPEAKER_01]: And for that very reason, you recognize a thing will cease.

595
00:43:48,660 --> 00:43:50,722
[SPEAKER_01]: Thus, a thing is impermanent.

